course: dictionary
lesson: 5381
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lots of words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. Knit has three meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant.
explain: «Gran knits you a jumper with a giant reindeer on it, and you hate it.» A jumper is a piece of clothing, so knits must mean makes clothes from wool. Try the meaning in the sentence to check: Gran makes you a jumper, and that makes sense.
explain: Knit can also be about your body. When a bone is broken, it knits together as it heals, so the two broken ends join and grow back as one. And «knit your brows» means to frown, so the brows do not get tied together in a knot.
fact: Knit means to make clothes or other things from wool or yarn by looping it together with two long needles or a machine.
fact: Knit can also mean that a broken bone joins and grows back together.
fact: «Knit your brows» means to frown.
fact: A knit is a knitted piece of clothing, such as a jumper.
fact: «A close-knit family» means a family who are very close to each other.
exercise: «Gran knits you a jumper with a giant reindeer on it.» What does knits mean? | Breaks into small pieces | *Makes clothes from wool by looping yarn with needles | Washes and dries clothes | Sells clothes in a shop
exercise: A broken arm knits together as it heals. What does knit mean here? | Pulls apart | *Joins and grows back together | Makes a jumper | Frowns at the pain
exercise: «She knit her brows when she read the bill.» What does knit her brows mean? | *Frowned | Closed her eyes | Smiled widely | Looked up at the sky
test: Jayden says his family is close-knit. What does close-knit mean? | A family who are cross with each other | A family with lots of pets | *A family who are very close to each other | A family who knit jumpers together every week
test: «Knitting and sewing needles are kept in a pincushion.» What kind of needles are these? | Needles for pricking balloons | Needles for mending bones | *Needles used to make clothes from wool or thread | Needles for frowning
exam: «Knitting machines have hundreds of tiny hooked needles that pull loops of yarn through other loops.» Which meaning of knit fits here? | *Making cloth by looping yarn together | Joining broken bones | Frowning hard | Going for a long walk
